"Assets must have unique names within their namespace (actions, baselines, traits, appearance features, encounters/encounter blobs, entity blobs, location-map themes, location maps, etc. -- each its own namespace) regardless of how the asset-update model evolves. A duplicate name is currently silent until it surfaces as a downstream failure (e.g. a unique-index insertion panic during map generation when two generated entities share a name). Validate uniqueness as EARLY as possible -- ideally at bundle authoring/build time and again on push_assets. Failure modes by environment: DEV mode = noisy, fail-fast (crash / loud error, ideally the client emits the error before pushing). PRODUCTION mode = tolerant: do not crash; log the violation to telemetry and continue (drop/last-wins the duplicate). Complements name-canonical-incremental-asset-updates (which relies on names as canonical keys) -- that task's dedupe/remap assumes this validation exists."